From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 17:59:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] test(linux-sandbox): run the root metadata fixture as UID 0
 and as the caller

The fixture's outer bubblewrap forced namespace UID/GID 0, so on hosted Ubuntu runners the inner sandbox's
nested UID map fails with "setting up uid map: Operation not permitted" and the whole test returned early,
which the harness reports as a pass.

Run every case once as namespace UID 0, as before, and once as the caller, each on a fresh fixture. Only the
UID 0 pass may skip on that refusal, with its own message; the caller pass always runs every assertion. The
fixture contents, permission profiles, scripts and assertions are unchanged.

Track: https://github.com/holdmyspot-com/codex-unleashed/issues/63
